# Question 0: towns without walls.
{300}{}{Is it true there's towns out there with no walls at all? Just houses, sitting in the open, like... like lunch?}
{301}{}{My village has none. Only a bridge and an old temple.}
{302}{}{A temple! With traps in? ...Billy says anything without a wall is just waiting its turn. I think yours sounds brave.}
{303}{}{Walls? We don't even have roofs. Too many giants.}
{304}{}{You're lying. [She squints at you.] ...How many giants?}
{305}{}{Ask somebody else.}
{306}{}{That's what everybody says. That's why I asked you.}

# Question 1: the biggest kill.
{310}{}{What's the biggest thing you ever killed? Stockholm shot a radscorpion once, but it was already limping.}
{311}{}{A giant ant. It was guarding a door.}
{312}{}{An ANT? How giant? Show me with your arms. Wider. ...That's a pretty good ant.}
{313}{}{A deathclaw. With a spoon.}
{314}{}{Nuh-uh. [A pause.] ...What kind of spoon?}
{315}{}{I don't keep count.}
{316}{}{I would. I'd keep a list. I'd put the ant first.}

# Question 2: vaults.
{320}{}{Do people really live under the ground, in big metal holes with doors like wheels? Billy saw a door like that once, in a mountain. Nobody was home.}
{321}{}{They do. The man who founded my village walked out of one.}
{322}{}{So you're a mole person! Only taller. Does the sun hurt? I bet it hurt him. I bet he squinted for a year.}
{323}{}{They do. They come out at night for children's teeth.}
{324}{}{They can have this one. I found it. It isn't mine.}
{325}{}{I wouldn't know.}
{326}{}{Nobody knows anything. I'm going to find one and knock.}

# Question 3: the bomb going off (only asked while it can).
{330}{}{If the bomb went off, would we go up or sideways? Harden says up. I say sideways, because of the walls.}
{331}{}{Neither. You'd just be gone, very fast.}
{332}{}{...Oh. [She thinks about it.] That's less fun than up.}
{333}{}{Up. You'd come down in Klamath.}
{334}{}{I KNEW it. Well. I said sideways. But I was thinking up.}
{335}{}{Don't think about that.}
{336}{}{Everybody thinks about it. They just don't say it. I say everything.}

# Question 4: are you staying.
{340}{}{Last one. Are you going to stay? People come in, and they're interesting, and then they go out the gate and they don't come back.}
{341}{}{I can't. I have people counting on me.}
{342}{}{That's what Billy said once. Then he stayed anyway. [She shrugs.] I'll save you some questions.}
{343}{}{I might. I hear there's an empty house.}
{344}{}{Then we'd be neighbors! Neighbors have to answer questions. It's a rule. I made it.}
{345}{}{Not if I can help it.}
{346}{}{You're grumpy. Doc Church is grumpy, and he's still here. So.}
{347}{}{I have a house here now. The one by the gate.}
{348}{}{Then we're neighbors! Neighbors have to answer questions. It's a rule. I made it.}

